			<div class="content" id="post-content-4848681">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> No</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> GoI format/Potential for separate SCP article on the prison and the Star of Bethlehem.</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> History, Horror, Action</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> GoI format/SCP article + addendums.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> Numerous SCPs undocumented by the foundation is located in the most unlikely place, The Vatican City. Beneath the city lies a 300-meter deep prison protected by powerful Templars, and priests known as Arminda's. The ancient prison contains SCPs via 'blessings' granted by the 'Star of Bethlehem' a large light orb at the top of the prison, which in itself is it's own SCP.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong>When foundation agents in Italy begin to vanish and remerge memoryless. The foundation is led to Vatican City.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Further&nbsp;Narrative</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Title&nbsp;for&nbsp;hiding&nbsp;text</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>To understand the cause of this, the foundation sent in an infiltration unit into the Vatican to watch for bizarre activity. Upon entering, the squad found nothing out of the ordinary, until they witnessed a man in white robes wall through a large display waterfall and vanish. The foundation now had proof of anomalous activity.</p>
<p>Concerned for a potential hostile threat, the SCP foundation conducted a full investigation into the activity. Including a squad sent to contain the white-robed priest- but yet again the squad failed to return, no bodies, no trace. Eventually, the foundation launched a full raid on the Vatican, and what they would uncover was The Sanctum, the Vatican's very own SCP Foundation, home to over 300 undocumented SCPs. In the center was a large pit traveling down 300 meters, and above was a bright ball of light that appeared to light the whole prison.</p>
<p>Upon entering, the foundation made contact with those who ran this facility. Ancient knights known as the Templars, and white-robed priests known as Armindas. Attempting to force entry brought hostility, and a fight broke out between the strike team and The Templars, who despite wielding only armor, swords, and shields, dispatched enough foundation units to force a retreat. From this point, The Sanctum is declared an enemy of The Foundation.</p>
<p>The story continues as the foundation attempts to decide whether to take the Sanctum by force or attempt to negotiate and uncover all of its secrets.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> I believe the idea has a lot of potentials to introduce new things the foundation never knew existed and uncover the true power that the Sanctum holds, and how it and the Foundation tetters on war or peace with each other. And the secret of what lies at the bottom of the prison, along with finding out how and why the Sanctum does such things.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> N/A</p>

